prompt:
Create one original true-transparent RGBA 5x3 row-major spritesheet of fifteen complete right-facing Moxie Capwell alley-oop-reverse poses. Moxie's supplied canon portrait/gameplay references define identity: adult human woman, pale skin, lavender-purple eyes, long thick lavender ponytail with small gold tie, mature athletic body, purple-and-silver uniform with white side panels, purple wristbands and high tops. Preserve exact face, anatomy, hair/tie and outfit in every view.

1990s arcade basketball pixel-cel art, crisp readable outlines. Exact 1536x1024 canvas, 15 separate complete figures, each centered with wide transparent margins/gutters and no clipping/overlap. True transparent RGBA. Moxie alone. Basketball remains separate gameplay art and is never drawn. No teammate, opponent, hoop/rim/net, court/floor, shadow, scenery, background, glow, effects, text or labels.

Alley-oop reverse dunk: Moxie receives a high lob, turns her back to the imaginary rim, then reaches behind her head to dunk backward on the far side.
0 cut toward the lob, eyes up;
1 plant to jump;
2 takeoff at tick4;
3 reach high with both hands;
4 receive lob at frame5/tick10 with right hand;
5 pull the separate ball close to shoulder;
6 twist hips and shoulders away, starting a reverse turn;
7 back faces the imaginary rim, right arm draws the ball behind her head;
8 rise with knees tucked and hand behind crown;
9 reach backward around the far side of her head;
10 extend into the reverse dunk and release at tick21;
11 score finish tick23, hand follows down behind the head;
12 rotate back toward right-facing view while descending;
13 land with knees bent;
14 stable athletic recovery.
Keep back and three-quarter-back poses readable but preserve Moxie's lavender ponytail/gold tie and purple/silver uniform. Full human anatomy, no ball or hoop drawn; both hands remain empty and visible.
